---
title: Pfeffernisse
author: Grandma Gustad
category: Cookies
source: Loving Memories of Mildred
---

@sugar{2%cups}
@honey{1.5%cups}
@butter{0.5%cup}
@eggs{3} (beat in one-at-a-time)
@cold coffee{0.75%cup}
@baking soda{1.5%tsp}
@black pepper{1%tsp}
@almond extract{0.5%tsp}
@flour{7%cups}
@baking powder{1%tsp}
@cloves{0.25%tsp}
@anise oil or flavoring{1.75%tsp}
@cinnamon{0.5%tsp}
@powdered sugar

Cook sugar, honey and butter for about 15 minutes and let cool. Add eggs - beat in one-at-a-time. Add cold coffee, baking soda, black pepper, almond extract, baking powder, cloves, anise oil or flavoring, cinnamon. Add flour to make a firm enough dough to drop. Bake at 350 degrees until brown. Cover with powdered sugar as soon as out of oven.
